module gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_rotation_route

import std.types { NonEmptyStr, String }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Terminal }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.bmc_implementation_dispatch {
  BmcRotationRoute,
  RotationRouteRedfishAccountService,
  RotationRouteUnavailable,
}
import gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure {
  CredentialRotationApplication,
  AccountManagementUnavailable,
}

// THIS ROW WAS A TYPE ERROR AND IT COMPILED ANYWAY (review 63271). It read
// `Disposition = SingleAuthority`, and SingleAuthority is an arm of ConstructionMechanism, not of
// Disposition -- which has exactly Terminal and Scaffold. Every other `: Disposition =` site in the
// corpus uses one of those two.
//
// THE REVIEW CALLED THE CONSEQUENCE "the module therefore does not compile". IT DOES COMPILE, and
// that is the worse finding rather than a lesser one. This session's own run resolved the closure
// containing this row and failed only on a wrong function name, and gunbc#10952 was green on all
// four required checks with the row present. The reason is a rostered below-floor defect: a wrong
// COPRODUCT value is accepted into a declared field with no diagnostic, while the same check fires
// for primitives and unresolved names. So the ordinary compiler floor -- "values inhabit declared
// types" (DESIGN §4b) -- did not hold, and a plainly wrong row rode four green checks.
//
// The value is Terminal because this module is not scaffolding: it holds one fold that binds a
// route to the application the adjudication refuses on, and there is no construction it dissolves
// into.
data bmc_rotation_route_disposition: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "The route-to-application binding is the terminal form: gunbc.bmc_implementation_dispatch decides the route by firmware family, and this module maps that route to the machine_intake CredentialRotationApplication the adjudication refuses on. Nothing here is staged pending a different construction." as NonEmptyStr,
}

// BINDING A ROUTE TO THE APPLICATION THE ADJUDICATION REFUSES ON. The family-keyed dispatch that
// picks the route is NOT here: it is gunbc.bmc_implementation_dispatch rotation_route_for_family,
// alongside the three other family-keyed folds.
//
// THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS MODULE OWNED THAT DISPATCH AND THAT WAS A FORK (review 63250). The
// block comment argued at length that a realization dispatch belongs peripheral to both extdeps
// modules rather than inside either -- which is correct DESIGN §3 reasoning and was the wrong
// conclusion, because the corpus had ALREADY built that peripheral home and the argument never
// mentioned it. gunbc.bmc_implementation_dispatch says of itself that a third implementation
// "refuses to compile here and nowhere else; that is the census", and a fourth `match family` over
// here falsified that sentence the moment it landed -- splitting the third-implementation census
// across two modules with no cross-reference between them. gunbc#9678 already paid for this exact
// fork once, in the other direction.
//
// SO THE DISPATCH MOVED AND THE SPLIT IS AT THE LAYER BOUNDARY, not at a convenience line. What is
// keyed on BmcFirmwareFamily and cites only extdeps.bmc facts went to the dispatch home. What
// remains here is the part that is not family-keyed at all: mapping a route to a machine_intake
// CredentialRotationApplication. Hoisting that would make the peripheral dispatch module import
// machine_intake and invert the layering it exists to keep straight.
//
// THE ROUTE IS KEYED ON AN OBSERVATION, NEVER ON AN EXPECTATION, and that constraint binds the
// caller of the dispatch rather than this fold. The family comes from a
// workflow-layer receipt -- for the held unit, gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_access_observation,
// which carries family AmiMegaRac with committed raw bytes and a digest, and which established
// Redfish absence against a discriminating control: five Redfish paths refused over TLS while the
// same host answered 200 on its web root, so "no Redfish service" is separated from "host
// unreachable". extdeps.ampere.mt_collins_product_brief.bmc holds only an EXPECTATION and forbids
// its own promotion; nothing here may read it, and this module never takes a family from it.

// THE REFUSAL IS PRODUCED BEFORE ANY CONTROLLER WRITE, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT OF PUTTING THE
// ROUTE AHEAD OF THE ATTEMPT. An unavailable route yields AccountManagementUnavailable, which
// gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure adjudicates into a typed, located BmcSecure refusal whose owner
// is derived rather than authored. It does not silently skip, and it is not filed as a hardware
// defect: bmc_secure_refusal_owner routes an access state to a PartsHold rather than to the return
// clock, because a firmware we cannot yet drive is not a defect of the unit the seller shipped.
//
// THE SENTENCE ABOVE IS ABOUT THE VALUE THIS FOLD RETURNS, NOT ABOUT ANY UNIT'S ARRIVAL PHASE, and
// the first draft of this block asserted the latter in the PRESENT TENSE (review 63236). It read
// "a unit whose firmware has no rotation transport FAILS ITS ARRIVAL PHASE and is never certified
// as secured". That is not true today and nothing here makes it true: BmcCredentialRotationObservation
// takes `rotation` as a SUPPLIED field, so no unit's arrival phase consults this table. The claim
// described the terminal architecture and wore the tense of the current one, which is DESIGN §4b(1)
// rung inflation -- the executed evidence is this module's witness fold and nothing else, and a
// sentence about arrival phases cited that evidence for a claim it does not support.

// WHO CONSUMES THIS TABLE, AND BY WHAT ROUTE (DESIGN §3c). Today: nobody in production. The only
// executing consumer of rotation_application_for_route is
// test.claim.machine_intake_bmc_rotation_route_witness_test, which exercises both arms
// rather than asserting they exist. That is the honest state and it is stated rather than left to
// be discovered, because a declaration whose consumption is described in a PR body and absent from
// the diff is exactly §3c's red.
//
// THIS IS THE ADMISSIBLE MIDDLE STATE -- consumed by a NAMED consumer landing in a NAMED later
// change -- and the trigger is stated here rather than borrowed from
// gunbc.bmc_implementation_dispatch megarac_rotation_route_frontier, which answers a different
// question: that row dissolves the UNAVAILABLE ARM and says nothing about whether any caller
// exists, so citing it for consumption would be one dissolution condition doing two jobs. (It was
// cited here as "the frontier below" until the arm it guards moved to the dispatch home, which is
// what DESIGN §3 means by naming the symbol rather than the position -- a positional citation is
// invalidated by an edit that never touches either end.)
data rotation_route_consumption_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when the effectful rotation actuator named in gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure -- the producer of BmcCredentialRotationObservation, gated on the gunbc.bmc_onboarding split -- derives the rotation field by calling rotation_application_for_route on the family read from the controller, rather than receiving it as a supplied argument; at that point a MegaRAC unit's Arrival phase genuinely fails on this table and the present-tense claim becomes authorable. NOT satisfied by this module typechecking, by the witness exercising both arms, or by any caller that passes a route it constructed itself rather than one this table returned" as NonEmptyStr,
)
fn rotation_application_for_route(route: BmcRotationRoute) -> CredentialRotationApplication? {
  match route {
    RotationRouteRedfishAccountService { transport_operation: _, action_shape: _ } => none
    RotationRouteUnavailable { family_note: f, detail: d } =>
      Present {
        value: AccountManagementUnavailable {
          detail: join([f as String, ": ", d as String], "") as NonEmptyStr,
        },
      }
  }
}
